select null, t.id, 'builtin', 'In Westgard multirule quality control, the 1-3s rule is violated when:', '["Two consecutive controls exceed the same ±2SD limit","One control result falls outside the mean ±3SD","One control exceeds +2SD and another exceeds −2SD in the same run","Ten consecutive results fall on one side of the mean"]'::jsonb, 1, '1-3s = a single control beyond ±3SD. It is a rejection rule and usually points to random error. 2-2s detects systematic error, R-4s random error within a run, and 10x a shift. Reference: Westgard QC, Westgard Rules (westgard.com/westgard-rules.html).', '["That is the 2-2s rule (systematic error).","A single control beyond ±3SD, usually random error. Reject the run.","That is the R-4s rule (random error).","That is the 10x rule (systematic error, a shift)."]'::jsonb, 2, 'verified'
